  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohit Gupta And Another vs Union Territory Of J&K on 27 November, 2020 Author: Sanjay Dhar Bench: Sanjay Dhar Sr. No. 110 High Court Of Jammu And Kashmir At Jammu (Through Virtual Mode) Crm(M) No.413/2020 CrlM No.1558 & 1559 of 2020 Mohit Gupta and another .....Petitioner(s) Through :- Mr. Sachin Gupta, Advocate V/s Union Territory of J&K .....Respondent(s) Through :- Coram: Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Sanjay Dhar, Judge Order",
    "facts": "Through the medium of instant petition, the petitioners have challenged FIR No.237/2020 for offences under Section 272, 273, 328, 420, 120-B of IPC, Section 7/16 of Food Safety Act and Section 3/7 of Essential Commodities Act registered with Police Station, Bari Brahmana. It is the case of the petitioners that the offences stated in the FIR are not made out from a bare reading of the contents of the said FIR, inasmuch as the petitioners are duly licensed and authorized to manufacture, re-pack and re-label Mustard oil and Soyabean oil. In this regard the petitioners Mohit Gupta And Another vs Union Territory Of J&K on 27 November, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/82226384/ 1 have placed on record copy of the licenses issued by the competent authority. It is the further case of the petitioners that during investigation of the case, the reports of the Food Analyst pertaining to the samples of Soyabean oil and Mustard oil seized from the factory of the petitioners have been found to be conforming to the standards. Copies of said reports have been placed on record.",
    "arguments": "",
